{"title":"University of South Carolina High School Math Contest/1993 Exam/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=University_of_South_Carolina_High_School_Math_Contest/1993_Exam/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If 3 circles of radius 1 are mutually tangent as shown, what is the area of the gap they enclose?\n</p>\n<center><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Usc93.3.PNG\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/9/90/Usc93.3.PNG\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"211\" height=\"192\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span></center>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/7/227f1a2b8eb2d0db348d77c1a333fd54147c86ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A) \\ }\\sqrt{3}-\\frac{\\pi}2 \\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ } \\frac 16 \\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\ }\\frac 13 \\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\ } \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}2 - \\frac{\\pi}6 \\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\ } \\frac{\\pi}6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"463\" height=\"41\" /></center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=University_of_South_Carolina_High_School_Math_Contest/1993_Exam/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We connect the centers of the three circles, and we get an equilateral triangle, composed of three congruent sectors and the gap in question. The area of the three gaps is half the area of one of the circles, and is thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/e/aeebb746f8c0d3dac5219c3635617032430afee9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"17\" height=\"34\" />. The area of the whole triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/2/6b2c7f722a8f814c686a0c5387e208c2371345f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2^2\\sqrt{3}}{4}=\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"93\" height=\"41\" />, so the area of the gap is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/7/e9798f76c95ee9ac473d53785ea9e9827c46481f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{3}-\\frac{\\pi}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"60\" height=\"33\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/2/ca2f4283cfd441270cb90bfd2cf89a533f3dde81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"26\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=University_of_South_Carolina_High_School_Math_Contest/1993_Exam/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=University_of_South_Carolina_High_School_Math_Contest/1993_Exam/Problem_2\" title=\"University of South Carolina High School Math Contest/1993 Exam/Problem 2\">Previous Problem</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=University_of_South_Carolina_High_School_Math_Contest/1993_Exam/Problem_4\" title=\"University of South Carolina High School Math Contest/1993 Exam/Problem 4\">Next Problem</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=University_of_South_Carolina_High_School_Math_Contest/1993_Exam\" title=\"University of South Carolina High School Math Contest/1993 Exam\">Back to Exam</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018043317\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expir